# Dichroic Cupertino (UBI design language)

Cupertino-grade minimalism + intentional immersive glass. Purple-blue dichroic mono only.

## ALLOW

- Deep indigo / twilight violet backgrounds: `#0B0620`, `#120A2E`, `#2A1650`, `#3D1F6E`
- Electric blue primary `#4F6BFF`; cyan glow `#5CE1FF` sparingly (LIVE edge only)
- Text `#F2F4FF` / muted `#A8B0D6`
- Borders `rgba(255,255,255,0.14)` micro-highlights
- Glass fills: strong `rgba(18,10,46,0.72)`, medium `0.55`, subtle `0.38`
- ONE primary frosted sheet; other chrome quieter
- Soft violet→blue ambient mesh blobs at low opacity
- System / SF-like / system-ui condensed titles; tracking −0.4 to −0.8 on display
- UI labels 600–700; padding 16–20
- Calm status rows (not shouty)

## BAN

- Rainbow neon, aurora spam, multi-hue glows
- Inter, Geist, or generic AI-default sans stacks as display faces
- Glass-on-every-card (frost only where it earns hierarchy)
- Barranco brick / dusty coral (`#A65A45`) as primary
- Hot mint LED, coral neon, champagne-brass chrome as the system
- Fake “live” pulse animations; heat rings only from real voyCommits

## Map

- Retheme sheet, scrubber, chips, Voy CTA to electricBlue / violet
- Solid primary Voy; optional cyan edge on LIVE only
- Esri dark (or darker) tiles; pin fills from dichroic accents

## Rule of one

One primary frosted surface per view. Prefer layered translucency + LinearGradient sheens over blur spam.
